  "question": {
    "text": "For the octahedral complexes of <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">F</mi><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup></math> in <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo></mrow></msup></math> (thiocyanato-S) and in <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo></mrow></msup></math> ligand environments, the difference between the spin-only magnetic moments in Bohr magnetons (when approximated to the nearest integer) is<br />[Atomic number of Fe = 26]"
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "4",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo></mrow></msup></math>  is weak field effect (WFE) ligand whereas  <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo></mrow></msup></math>  is strong field effect (SFE) ligand.<br > <br/><img src=\"assets\\st0023_e6b604daf5ab.png\"/> <br >        Spin only magnetic moment  <math><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mn>5</mn><mo>(</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>)</mo></msqrt><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mn>35</mn></msqrt><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"> </mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi></math> <br > <br/><img src=\"assets\\st0023_e9a60d24a9b0.png\"/> <br >        Spin only magnetic moment  <math><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mn>1</mn><mo>(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>)</mo></msqrt><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"> </mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi></math> <br >        Difference  <math><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mn>35</mn></msqrt><mo>-</mo><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"> </mi><mo>≃</mo><mn>4</mn></math>"
